Flow diagram: what happens when you type https://www.google.com and press Enter

+------------------+
|     BROWSER      |
|  www.google.com  |
+--------+---------+
         |
         | 1. DNS RESOLUTION
         v
+------------------+       +-------------------+       +--------------------+
|   DNS RESOLVER   | ----> | ROOT / TLD SERVER | ----> | GOOGLE NAMESERVER  |
|  (ISP / Router)  |       |    (.com, etc.)    |       | returns 142.250.x.x|
+--------+---------+       +-------------------+       +--------------------+
         |
         | IP address returned to browser
         |
         | 2. TCP CONNECTION (port 443)
         |    SYN -> SYN-ACK -> ACK
         |
         | 3. FIREWALL CHECK
         v
+------------------+
|    FIREWALL      |
|  allows port 443 |
+--------+---------+
         |
         | 4. HTTPS / TLS ENCRYPTION
         |    Certificate verified
         |    Session key exchanged
         |    All traffic encrypted
         v
+------------------+
|  LOAD BALANCER   |
|  distributes     |
|  traffic across  |
|  server pool     |
+--------+---------+
         |
         +-------------------------+
         |                         |
         v                         v
+------------------+     +------------------+
|   WEB SERVER     |     |   WEB SERVER     |
|   (nginx)        |     |   (nginx)        |
|  serves static   |     |  serves static   |
|  assets          |     |  assets          |
+--------+---------+     +------------------+
         |
         | dynamic request forwarded
         v
+------------------+
| APPLICATION      |
|    SERVER        |
|  runs business   |
|  logic / search  |
+--------+---------+
         |
         | queries data
         v
+------------------+
|    DATABASE      |
|  (Bigtable /     |
|   Spanner)       |
|  returns results |
+--------+---------+
         |
         | response travels back up the chain
         v
+------------------+
|     BROWSER      |
|  renders the     |
|  HTML page       |
+------------------+

Full flow summary:
  Browser
    -> DNS resolution (domain -> IP)
    -> TCP handshake on port 443
    -> Firewall (traffic allowed)
    -> TLS handshake (traffic encrypted)
    -> Load balancer (request distributed)
    -> Web server (static assets or forward)
    -> Application server (page generated)
    -> Database (data fetched)
    -> Response back to browser
